{
  "id": "inlay_hints/other_kinds/02_ctad_arguments",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "other_kinds",
  "title": "Deduced class template arguments",
  "summary": "A class template whose arguments its initialization deduces shows them",
  "prose": "The arguments follow the template's name wherever it is written without them: a declaration, a functional cast, a `new`; they print as the template's own name takes them, whatever scope encloses it and whatever aliases or defaults a deduction guide wrote. A variable initialized by such a cast shows no type of its own while the arguments say it.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#2331"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename A, typename B>\nstruct Pair {\n    A first;\n    B second;\n    Pair(A a, B b);\n};\n\nPair pair(1, 2.5);\nauto copy = Pair(3, 'c');\nauto* heap = new Pair(4, 5);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nusing same = T;\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Holder {\n    Holder(T value);\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nHolder(T) -> Holder<same<T>>;\n\nauto held = Holder(6);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nusing Twin = Pair<T, T>;\n\nTwin twin(7, 8);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Outer {\n    template <typename U>\n    struct Inner {\n        Inner(U item);\n    };\n};\n\nOuter<int>::Inner inner(1.5);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Traits {};\n\ntemplate <typename T, typename Tr = Traits<T>>\nstruct Text {\n    Text(const T* source);\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nText(const T*) -> Text<T, Traits<T>>;\n\nText text(\"abc\");\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
